@@ -1,5 +1,17 @@
 # Web search: discovery and verification
 
+## Automatic publication
+
+**Refresh events** searches and automatically publishes eligible discoveries every day at 09:23 London time. To run it on demand, select **Discover new** when starting **Refresh events**. The separate **Test event discovery** workflow is a diagnostic and is not needed for publication.
+
+The automatic path uses the existing Brave secret and up to 12 queries per run, or 372 scheduled queries in a 31-day month. Manual discovery and diagnostics are additional. Results are leads: it checks up to 24 direct listings on recognised booking platforms or configured organiser sites. Each new record needs an unambiguous structured event on the listing itself, an exact future start time, a named venue in London, UK, a recognised topic and an in-stock or limited-availability offer linking to a verified type of booking page. Redirects, catalogues, unknown domains, online-only events, incomplete details and restricted-audience listings are skipped. An independent organiser can qualify through its Eventbrite, Luma or Ticket Tailor listing.
+
+The same build checks current feeds, published and archived events, and its own discovery history. It blocks duplicate IDs, matching source URLs or listing IDs, and matching titles on the same London date. The default limit is five new and 20 active automatic listings. A run can correctly publish zero. GitHub Actions logs the counts and skip reasons; no approval step is required.
+
+Daily runs recheck active automatic listings directly without calling Brave. If a page no longer verifies, its listing is omitted on the next successful refresh; if the original event verifies again it can reappear. Completed events follow the normal archive process. The production workflow commits the event dataset and the discovery history together. If the Brave request fails, that discovery run leaves the last publication in place; normal daily runs use no Brave credentials.
+
+The sections below describe the separate discovery diagnostic and its legacy import path.
+
 There are three different kinds of search in London Data Radar:
 
 | Feature | What it does | When it runs |
